Returns everything an LLM needs about a symbol (or package) in one query.

Symbol mode combines definition, references, callers, callees, role, and purpose.
Package mode returns exports, imports, dependent count, LOC, tests, and key types.

Multi-ID mode bundles multiple symbols in one response:
  snipe pack abc123def456 789012345678  # Multiple hex IDs

Examples:
  snipe pack ProcessOrder              # Symbol profile by name
  snipe pack --at main.go:42:12        # Symbol profile at position
  snipe pack Handler --refs-limit 5    # Limit references returned
  snipe pack internal/mcp              # Package profile
  snipe pack ./internal/store          # Package profile (relative path)

Usage:
  snipe pack [symbol|package...] [flags]

Flags:
      --at string           Position to look up (file:line:col)
      --callees-limit int   Maximum callees to return (default 5)
      --callers-limit int   Maximum callers to return (default 5)
  -h, --help                help for pack
      --refs-limit int      Maximum references to return (default 5)

Global Flags:
      --context int        Context lines around match (default 2)
      --format string      concise | detailed | summary | json | human (default "concise")
      --kg-hints           Include Orca KG hints
      --limit int          Cap results (default 10)
      --max-tokens int     Token budget (0 = unlimited)
      --no-body            Exclude function body
      --no-siblings        Exclude sibling declarations
      --offset int         Pagination offset
      --select string      Result selection: all, best, top3, top5 (default "all")
      --signature-only     Return only signature (no body, no context)
      --suggestions        Include next-step suggestions in Claude output
      --timeout duration   Timeout for command (e.g., 30s, 5m)
